Rules:
  [M1] Use `_id` as primary key (auto-generated ObjectId).
  [M2] Use embedded documents for one-to-few relationships.
  [M3] Use references for one-to-many or many-to-many.
  [M4] Use proper data types (ISODate, ObjectId).
  [M5] Use `$set` for partial updates.
  [M6] Use `$push` for array operations.
  [M7] Use `$lookup` for joins (sparingly).
  [M8] Use `$text` for full-text search.

Pros:
  - Flexible schema
  - Horizontal scaling
  - JSON-like documents

Cons:
  - No joins (limited)
  - Memory usage
  - Consistency model

Alternatives:
  - PostgreSQL (ACID)
  - CouchDB (HTTP API)
  - DynamoDB (managed)

State: +

